draw((-10,0)--(-5,8.7)--(5,8.7)--(10,0)--cycle);
draw((-5,8.7)--(0,0)--(5,8.7));
draw(anglemark((-5,8.7),(0,0),(-10,0),30));
draw(anglemark((5,8.7),(0,0),(-5,8.7),35));
draw(anglemark((10,0),(0,0),(5,8.7),30));
[/asy]

Let $E$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $B$ to $\overline{CD}$. Then $AB = DE$ and $BE =
AD = 7$. By the Pythagorean Theorem, \begin{align*}
AD^2 = BE^2 &= BC^2 - CE^2\\
&= (CD+AB)^2 - (CD - AB)^2\\
&=(CD+AB+CD-AB)(CD+AB-CD+AB)\\
&=4\cdot CD \cdot AB.
\end{align*}Hence, $AB \cdot CD = AD^2/4=7^2/4=49/4=\boxed{12.25}$.

