label("3",(-3/2,-7/8),S);
label("3",(3/2,-7/8),S);
[/asy] By the Pythagorean theorem, the altitude shown is $\sqrt{5^2-3^2}=4$.

Now we can draw and label a radius of the circle: [asy]
unitsize(20);
draw(Circle((0,0),25/8));
draw(((-3,-7/8)--(3,-7/8)--(0,25/8)--cycle));
dot((0,0));
draw(((0,25/8)--(0,0)),dotted);
